  "content": {
    "id": "v2-1ddc9-p55-practice-slot-10-lower-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Solve each of these equations for $0\\leq x<360^{\\circ}$ to the nearest degree.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 3,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "v2-1ddc9-p55-practice-slot-10-lower-slot-10-lower-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{1}{\\sin x}=2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=30^{\\circ}$ or $150^{\\circ}$; $\\sin x=\\frac{1}{2}$, Q1 and Q2.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{1}{\\sin x}&=2\\\\1&=2\\sin x\\\\\\sin x&=\\frac{1}{2}\\\\A&=\\sin^{-1}\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\\\A&=30^{\\circ}\\end{align*}$$\nSine is positive in Q1 and Q2.\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=30^{\\circ}\\\\x&=180^{\\circ}-30^{\\circ}\\\\x&=150^{\\circ}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 35
      },
      {
        "id": "v2-1ddc9-p55-practice-slot-10-lower-slot-10-lower-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{3}{\\cos x}=-5$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x\\approx127^{\\circ}$ or $233^{\\circ}$; $\\cos x=-\\frac{3}{5}$, Q2 and Q3.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{3}{\\cos x}&=-5\\\\3&=-5\\cos x\\\\\\cos x&=-\\frac{3}{5}\\\\A&=\\cos^{-1}\\left(\\frac{3}{5}\\right)\\end{align*}$$\nCosine is negative in Q2 and Q3. Using the unrounded value of $A$:\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=180^{\\circ}-A\\\\x&\\approx127^{\\circ}\\\\x&=180^{\\circ}+A\\\\x&\\approx233^{\\circ}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      },
      {
        "id": "v2-1ddc9-p55-practice-slot-10-lower-slot-10-lower-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{1}{\\tan x}=4$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x\\approx14^{\\circ}$ or $194^{\\circ}$; $\\tan x=\\frac{1}{4}$, Q1 and Q3.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{1}{\\tan x}&=4\\\\1&=4\\tan x\\\\\\tan x&=\\frac{1}{4}\\\\A&=\\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac{1}{4}\\right)\\end{align*}$$\nTangent is positive in Q1 and Q3. Using the unrounded value of $A$:\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=A\\\\x&\\approx14^{\\circ}\\\\x&=180^{\\circ}+A\\\\x&\\approx194^{\\circ}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      }
    ]
  },
